        "summary": "Fixed the alias handling in traitlets.config.application.Application to properly support aliases with tuples of any length, not just 2-element tuples. The issue was in the _flatten_aliases method where:\n\n1. Line 737 incorrectly assumed longname tuples had exactly 2 elements: `longname, _ = longname`\n2. Line 748 had a typo checking `aliases` instead of `alias` and flawed logic\n\nChanged the code to:\n- Extract the first element from longname tuples: `longname = longname[0]` \n- Properly check if alias is a tuple: `if not isinstance(alias, tuple):`\n\nThis restores support for multiple aliases per flag as documented and demonstrated by the test_aliases_multiple test case.",
